{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/815057-shards","id":815057,"title":"Shards","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-23T14:53:46-08:00","id":815057,"title":"Shards","content":"I got an idea, but I need help refining it. I like the concept of a smaller simpler, weaker, demonic being. It may have been weak to begin with, or I'm thinking, perhaps it was the results of a brutal Fall, where the demon was smashed to Shards.<br /> In any case, these would be mechanical beings protected by cover, just like demons. However, they would be weaker (fewer demonic form powers, embeds etc) and less impressive (less attributes and skills). They would have the covers of animals, but intellects that could be on the level of a human child. <br /> Basically, they are simple allies or enemies. They could be a raven made from the hand of a fallen angel, and that demonic shard spends its days eating carrion and spying on a demon in the suburbs out of sheer fascination, using its instrumental embed at times. They could be a dog made from a failed Angel summoning, and it performs its guardian duties by attacking anyone that comes close to its building using its demonic form if necessary.<br /> I realize that slivers and shards are similar, and perhaps I should just use the sliver concept and evolve it. I'm looking for something slightly different though. Demons in the shapes of animals. <br /> Thoughts on rules or cool ideas on Shards, people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5260,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5260-themangynimrod","user":"TheMangyNimrod","date":". 01-23-2016, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5260-themangynimrod","name":"TheMangyNimrod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:47:39-08:00","id":815082,"title":"","content":"Cryptids already exist to fill this niche, and do so nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:52:01-08:00","id":820815,"title":"","content":"I see no reason to limit them to animal forms- fully powered angels and demons can already have animal covers, or heck, even inanimate objects as covers. <br /> <br /> In fact I would think a demon stuck in the form of a gun for example would probably envy those with an animal cover. <br /> <br /> I'm surprised you didn't go with the idea of naming them Imp though, it's certainly what springs to my mind with the phrase &quot;like a demon but weaker.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:59:02-08:00","id":820818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/815057-shards?p=820815#post820815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised you didn't go with the idea of naming them Imp though, it's certainly what springs to my mind with the phrase &quot;like a demon but weaker.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Imps are already a different thing; they're functionally Rank 1 angels without the personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:31:37-08:00","id":827047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/815057-shards?p=820818#post820818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imps are already a different thing; they're functionally Rank 1 angels without the personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>So an Fallen Imperative perchance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:40:50-08:00","id":827055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/815057-shards?p=827047#post827047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So an Fallen Imperative perchance?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like they're not enough of a person to Fall, so they just malfunction instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:26:24-08:00","id":827092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/815057-shards?p=827055#post827055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds like they're not enough of a person to Fall, so they just malfunction instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it doesn't have to take willful disobedience to Fall, hell an angel can do it's job perfectly and still potentially fall because it then didn't come home fast enough. That said, Imperatives as a whole seem to lack the cognizance of a sapient being to begin with, so perhaps an Imp is a result of what happens when an Imperative ( see what I did there? hahah) malfunctions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 02-09-2016, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}